  "styleGuide": "PALETTE: walls spruce_planks, birch_planks (clapboard), bricks for shops; trim dark_oak_planks, stripped_dark_oak_log; roofs deepslate_tiles, dark_oak_stairs; foundations cobblestone, mossy_cobblestone; floors oak_planks, dark_oak_planks; windows glass_pane in spruce trapdoor frames; doors spruce_door; chimneys bricks, cobblestone; fences white birch_fence, spruce_fence; lamps lantern on spruce_fence posts.\nSHAPES: steep gable and gambrel roofs, 4-block storeys, small-paned windows in rows, covered front porches, widow's walks on rich houses.\nINTERIORS: plank floors with carpets, wainscot (stripped logs), fireplaces of bricks, oil lamps (lanterns), heavy dark furniture.\nWEAR AND MOOD: salt-greyed wood, moss on foundations, fog-dark windows, a few cracked bricks.\nBY BUILDING: church white birch with a spire; shops red brick with false fronts; inn two storeys with a long porch; lighthouse white with a red band.\nAVOID: concrete, quartz, bright modern colours, sea lanterns outside the lighthouse."
